# Ephemeral test dirs created at repo root by Jest suites
# Nested framework installs created by installer/e2e tests.
# These are full framework copies; without this they pollute ESLint and Jest
# (roots: [<rootDir>]) with phantom files, and a single `git add .` would commit them.
#
# Every project name our own documentation suggests to `init` is listed here.
# The list only had /my-project/, so any reader who followed a different page
# ended up with an untracked ~8,600-file framework copy that ESLint and Jest
# (roots: [<rootDir>]) swept — the gates then reported hundreds of errors and
# phantom suites against a tree whose own code has none.
#
# Sourced from: git grep -oE "init [a-z][a-z0-9-]{2,30}" -- docs/ README*.md
# Re-run that after adding an install page, or this hole reopens.
/AEXOS/
/my-project/          # README.md, docs/installation/*, 12 occurrences
/my-first-project/    # docs/getting-started.md
/myapp/               # docs/troubleshooting.md
/test/                # docs/troubleshooting.md — no root test/ exists (tests/ does)
/.aexos-test/
.test-temp*/
#
# Deliberately NOT listed: /pro/. The grep also matches "init pro", but those
# are `git submodule update --init pro` in docs/guides/workflows/ — not a
# project name — and pro/ is a real submodule directory. Ignoring it would hide
# the Pro edition from git.

# Python bytecode from the .claude/hooks/*.py governance hooks.
# Six .pyc files were committed during the rebrand; untracked and ignored here.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

